    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "staring at a ceiling doesn't change the fact that i have to go back to it tomorrow. it's all just a distraction. the machine always wins. it feels like the only way to actually \"step outside\" is to just... not be a part of it anymore. like, is there even any point in trying to reclaim yourself when the system is designed to just consume you until you're gone?",
